 "result_text": "I changed `get_adapted_type` in `src/sqlacodegen/generators.py` so MySQL `DOUBLE(11,2)` is no longer turned into `Double(11, True)`. I didn't run it against MySQL or add a test for this case. The existing test suite passes (94 passed).\n\n**Cause:** When generic `Double` is substituted for the MySQL type, the scale is lost, so the compiled SQL no longer matches `DOUBLE(11, 2)`. The code deliberately ignores that mismatch for `Float` types (and arrays of them), because on PostgreSQL `Float` can stand for both REAL and DOUBLE_PRECISION. That exception ran on every dialect, so MySQL got `Double(11, True)` too.\n\n**Fix:** The exception now applies only on PostgreSQL. On other dialects, a mismatch means the original type is kept. I expect MySQL to keep its own `DOUBLE` class, which retains the scale, rather than the generic `Double`.\n\nI didn't check what other dialects with a `Float` mismatch now render. They will also keep their original type, not generic `Float`/`Double`.",
